findings.trigger:
(a) any overload run (R1, R2, r3, r7, r9, r10, r12, r16a, r16b, r16e, r20, r21);
(b) r8a: a caller abandoning in RINGBACK in the same ms as the callee's first bell;
(c) r12: +trunc_nd=1;
(d) r20, r21, r22: 2 each;
(e) a load step with the shared harness.

findings.consequence:
(a) STUCK what=marker_state lines, each followed by STUCK-END, with no leak;
(b) 'WRONGRING t=3274 at=B75 caller=B44 dialled=B75 calling=0': the right caller on the right line;
(c) 15 DTAGAIN, the phones hanging up 100 ms after the key;
(d) network 'BUSY' outcomes that were really C15 refusals;
(e) recovery masked for one old idle mean.
None of these is an exchange fault.

findings.fix:
(a) reset the watch at each attach and flag one caller holding the register past 6*NODIG;
(b) let calling() keep a caller for phantom_grace after its hang-up when c_dest==g;
(c) ignore steady 1 in POST for ID+20 ms after a one-digit dial;
(d) classify an unattributed refusal as NOGO;
(e) re-draw idle phones at the step, as overload/load_harness.svh +switch_redraw=1 does.
All are harness edits.
